{"format":1,"key":"zone:ungoro","path":"/lore/zone/ungoro","name":"Un'Goro Crater","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"ungoro","name":"Un'Goro Crater","path":"/lore/zone/ungoro"},"levels":"","description":"Un'Goro Crater is a sunken, primordial jungle tucked between the arid wastes of Tanaris and Silithus. Dominated by roaming dinosaurs, living elementals…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:ungoro","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Un'Goro Crater is a sunken, primordial jungle tucked between the arid wastes of Tanaris and Silithus. Dominated by roaming dinosaurs, living elementals, and a central volcano, this lush caldera is filled with ancient Titan relics and power crystals whose origins remain a profound mystery.","Sandwiched between desert expanses, Un'Goro Crater defies the geography of southern Kalimdor. Ancient night elf records detailing the War of the Shifting Sands note that the insectoid Qiraji were turned back at the crater's edges, unable to penetrate what their tongue named the 'God Lands.' Scholars theorize the caldera served as a testing ground or ancient dwelling for the Titans during the shaping of Kalimdor. Stone pylons rise along the ridges, humming with energy, while crystal formations of blue, red, green, and yellow sprout through the primeval earth.","Un'Goro contains no cities, towns, or native humanoid societies. Instead, life thrives in an untamed, primeval state. Apex devilsaurs stalk the flats of Terror Run, predatory bloodpetals lash out in the marshlands, and oozes creep across the tar pits of Lakkari. At the heart of the crater looms Fire Plume Ridge, an active volcanic peak teeming with hostile fire elementals led by the entity Blazerunner. For explorers and skinners, the basin offers unmatched natural wealth—including the coveted hides of devilsaurs—provided one survives the food chain.","Civilized presence in the crater is limited almost entirely to Marshal's Refuge, an elevated camp tucked into the northern cliffs. Led by Williden Marshal, an expedition of scientists, naturalists, and fortune seekers attempted to catalogue the basin's treasures only to be battered by the monstrous wildlife and driven to high ground. Today, the refuge serves as an embattled staging ground for intrepid travelers studying the crater's mysterious power crystals, mapping volcanic activity, and keeping a watchful eye on encroaching silithid swarms breaching the southern ridges."],"hash":"10ee3a","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"381648ef94","sec":118},"female-narrator":{"sha":"6cfcce8d60","sec":128}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Un'Goro Crater (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Un'Goro_Crater_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Un'Goro Crater","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Un'Goro_Crater"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/marshal-s-refuge","n":"Marshal's Refuge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/fire-plume-ridge","n":"Fire Plume Ridge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakkari-tar-pits","n":"Lakkari Tar Pits","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/terror-run","n":"Terror Run","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/tanaris","n":"Tanaris","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/silithus","n":"Silithus","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/williden-marshal","n":"Williden Marshal","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/topic/titan","n":"Titan","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/quest/4513-a-little-slime-goes-a-long-way","n":"A Little Slime Goes a Long Way","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/bag-of-empty-ooze-containers","n":"Bag of Empty Ooze Containers","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/item/filled-pure-sample-jar","n":"Filled Pure Sample Jar","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/gadgetzan","n":"Gadgetzan","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/fire-plume-ridge","n":"Fire Plume Ridge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/fungal-rock","n":"Fungal Rock","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/golakka-hot-springs","n":"Golakka Hot Springs","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakkari-tar-pits","n":"Lakkari Tar Pits","k":"subzone"}